nio: keep the PID1 priority boost inside the run queue bounds

CI 644 panicked in _run_queue_enqueue+0x44 (lr
_sched_amp_processor_enqueue+0x3c) after BOOST.  The boost set
sched_pri/base_pri to MAXPRI_KERNEL + 1 = 96, but the non-realtime run
queue is indexed by sched_pri with NRQS = BASEPRI_REALTIME = 96, so the
legal indices are 0..95; rq->queues[96] is out of bounds and produced
the data abort (FAR=0).

Use MAXPRI_KERNEL (95), the highest legal index, which still outranks
the boot thread.  No other behaviour change.


diff --git a/osfmk/kern/sched_prim.c b/osfmk/kern/sched_prim.c
index 84f7270..e67b66c 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/sched_prim.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/sched_prim.c
@@ -401,8 +401,12 @@ nio_boost_pid1_and_preempt(void)
 	if (nio_pid1_thread == THREAD_NULL) {
 		return;
 	}
-	nio_pid1_thread->sched_pri = MAXPRI_KERNEL + 1;
-	nio_pid1_thread->base_pri = MAXPRI_KERNEL + 1;
+	/* CI 644 used MAXPRI_KERNEL + 1 (96), but the non-realtime run
+	 * queue has indices 0..95; run_queue_enqueue() indexed
+	 * rq->queues[96] and took a data abort.  MAXPRI_KERNEL (95) is
+	 * the highest legal index and still outranks the boot thread. */
+	nio_pid1_thread->sched_pri = MAXPRI_KERNEL;
+	nio_pid1_thread->base_pri = MAXPRI_KERNEL;
 	ast_on(AST_PREEMPT | AST_URGENT);
 }
 
